:name: CAN bench
:description: Three Zephyr nodes on one CAN bus, bridged to a host SocketCAN interface.

using sysbus

# Every node is the same board. Only the firmware differs.
$repl?=@platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl
$vcu?=@/elf/vcu.elf
$bms?=@/elf/bms.elf
$dcdc?=@/elf/dcdc.elf

# The bus. Every node's CAN controller joins this hub.
emulation CreateCANHub "canHub"

# Two lines repeat on every machine.
#
# `showAnalyzer usart3` routes that node's Zephyr console to stdout, so
# `docker compose logs renode` shows each node booting. Without it a node's
# printk goes nowhere and the only evidence it ran is frames on the bus.
#
# `logLevel 3 nvic` drops the NVIC to errors only. Zephyr maintains the D-cache
# on this part by writing registers Renode does not model, and each write logs
# a warning: 134,221 of them in 56 minutes on one run, 99.9% of everything the
# container printed.
mach create "vcu"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $repl
logLevel 3 nvic
showAnalyzer usart3
sysbus LoadELF $vcu
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan1 canHub

mach create "bms"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $repl
logLevel 3 nvic
showAnalyzer usart3
sysbus LoadELF $bms
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan1 canHub

mach create "dcdc"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $repl
logLevel 3 nvic
showAnalyzer usart3
sysbus LoadELF $dcdc
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan1 canHub

# One bridge only: two bridges on one vcan interface loop frames forever.
mach set "vcu"
machine CreateSocketCANBridge "socketcan" "vcan0"
connector Connect socketcan canHub

# Both values were measured on this bench rather than copied from an example.
#
# Without serial execution, nodes stop transmitting at random with no error
# reported, and throughput varied between 28% and 100% of real time across
# identical runs.
#
# At 100 us the three nodes stay within 4 ms of each other. 25 us, which
# upstream's two-machine example uses, costs about 23% of throughput (measured:
# 190 vs 247 DCDC_Status frames in 60 s); 1 ms spreads the nodes 76 ms apart and
# 10 ms spreads them 285 ms.
emulation SetGlobalSerialExecution True
emulation SetGlobalQuantum "0.0001"

start
